<title>USA: Twin Disc Q1 order backlog up over Q4.</title>
<headline>Twin Disc Q1 order backlog up over Q4.</headline>
<dateline>RACINE, Wis. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twin Disc Inc said Friday its backlog of new orders to be shipped in the next six months at September 30 stood at $71 million, up eight percent from the June 30 fourth quarter.</p>
<p>But it said the backlog was the same as that reported a year ago.</p>
<p>The recent increase was caused primarily by the scheduled buildup of requirements in a transmission contract. &quot;Shipping levels should continue to show improvement through the next three to six months,&quot; said chairman Michael Batten in a statement.</p>
<p>	    -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
